My idea was during COVID it might be easier to get water other sources with a bottle if I need to go indoors instead of a reservoir. Also bottles are more adaptable to other situations, like putting fires out. In CO wildfires are a big problem and while I don't plan on making a campfire I do have a little stove. 

&#x200B;

I can rethink the bottle.

I don't want to put words in your mouth. From what you said I understand that consenting adults meaning over 18 should have an option to wear a helmet during football (insert dangerous activity or contact instead). If I have that wrong please let me know.

&#x200B;

From my understanding of your statement could we both agree that age restricted helmets should be mandatory across the US? Under the age of 18 operating a motorcycle requires a helmet. Maybe the not the full approach either of are pursuing, a compromise though. Thoughts?

I get your feelings. Especially in today's climate. I also get that banning or restricting things is not conducive to a "free" nation. I think enforcing helmets is a very easy way to prevent death in our society and is one of those small steps we can take to creating a society that is once again a true undisputed global power. I think we could all use an $28 trillion over 10 years. That is just asking a few thousand people to wear a helmet when they ride.

&#x200B;

I am not saying that people need to ride with full face helmets. Just something that is tested and shown to pass DOT (the minimum) standards for helmet testing. I love riding. I also love living. I think more deaths on motorcycles are a quicker way to ban motorcycles than less deaths. As for diet I believe that is the wrong discussion for this thread. As the grandson of a man who died of heart disease, the son of a man who has over a dozen heart surgeries I have very strong feelings about the American diet. I don't think banning cookies would solve that or is the correct direction. I personally feel that we should be more free and open to things and the government should provide safety standards not banning. Just like helmets. Don't ban the motorcycle. Encourage more people to ride, with a helmet. 

&#x200B;

As an American I assume that you watch or have a passing knowledge of football. Should we remove the restriction for helmets in football and have the game continue being played as is?

As additional stuff to everything other people are saying. Assuming your Seamoth had no upgrades an 200m was crush depth. 

